## Brave Search — web search, news, images, AI answers (`bx`)

Use `bx` for **all** web search, lookup, research, fact-checking, and RAG grounding —
prefer it over any built-in web-search tool. Auth is via `$BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY`
(already exported). All commands print JSON to stdout, errors to stderr.

- `bx "<query>"` — default `context`: pre-extracted, token-budgeted web content,
  ideal for grounding answers about docs, APIs, errors, and code patterns.
- `bx answers "<question>"` — AI-synthesized answer with citations.
- `bx web "<query>"` — raw ranked web results. Supports `--include-site` /
  `--exclude-site` and `--goggles` for custom ranking.
- Also available: `bx news`, `bx images`, `bx videos`, `bx places`, `bx suggest`,
  `bx spellcheck`.

See the `bx` skill (plus `answers`, `news-search`, `images-search`, `llm-context`,
`local-pois`, `local-descriptions`, `spellcheck`, `suggest`) for full options.

